---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Solar Installation Nigeria for Home | Harmattan Solar Co"
  description="Solar for home and solar installation in Nigeria: compare written quotes from independent installers in Lagos, Abuja, Port Harcourt, Ibadan, Benin City, Enugu."
  canonical="https://harmattansolar.com/"
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@type": ["ProfessionalService", "LocalBusiness"], "@id": "https://harmattansolar.com/#organization", "name": "Harmattan Solar Co", "url": "https://harmattansolar.com", "logo": {"@type": "ImageObject", "url": "https://harmattansolar.com/images/og-image.webp"}, "priceRange": "$$", "telephone": "+234 809 000 0000", "email": "info@harmattansolar.com", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "addressLocality": "Lagos", "addressRegion": "Nigeria", "addressCountry": "NG"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 6.5244, "longitude": 3.3792}, "areaServed": [{"@type": "City", "name": "Lagos", "addressRegion": "Nigeria"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Lagos", "addressRegion": "Lagos State"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Abuja", "addressRegion": "FCT"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Port Harcourt", "addressRegion": "Rivers State"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Ibadan", "addressRegion": "Oyo State"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Benin City", "addressRegion": "Edo State"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Enugu", "addressRegion": "Enugu State"}], "@context": "https://schema.org", "description": "Solar for home and solar installation in Nigeria: compare written quotes from independent installers in Lagos, Abuja, Port Harcourt, Ibadan, Benin City, Enugu.", "image": "https://harmattansolar.com/images/og-image.webp", "hasOfferCatalog": {"@type": "OfferCatalog", "name": "Solar Installation Services", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "Offer", "itemOffered": {"@type": "Service", "name": "Home Solar Installation"}}, {"@type": "Offer", "itemOffered": {"@type": "Service", "name": "Inverter and Battery Installation"}}, {"@type": "Offer", "itemOffered": {"@type": "Service", "name": "Commercial Solar"}}, {"@type": "Offer", "itemOffered": {"@type": "Service", "name": "Solar and Inverter Repair"}}]}}</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "WebSite", "@id": "https://harmattansolar.com/#website", "url": "https://harmattansolar.com", "name": "Harmattan Solar Co", "publisher": {"@id": "https://harmattansolar.com/#organization"}}</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "How much does solar for a home cost in Nigeria, and how is it scoped?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It depends on the load you want to run, so an installer scopes it from the rating plates of your own appliances before quoting. For reference, Mercury Direct listed a 3.5 kVA hybrid inverter with 5 kWh of lithium and 8 x 450 W panels, installation included, at N3,400,000 in October 2026, and SMK Solar listed a 3.5 kVA, 5 kWh lithium and 6 x 450 W package at N3,121,000 (its page mentions installation accessories, so check whether labour is included). BusinessDay put 3-4 kVA systems at N2-3 million in February 2026. Naira prices move with the exchange rate, so a current written quote is the real number."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How quickly will an installer respond, and how long does installation take?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "This site does not publish a guaranteed response or installation time, because the schedule belongs to the installer who quotes your job. Ask for the survey date and the installation schedule to be written on the proposal. A vague timeline on paper is a reason to compare with another quote."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Will a 3.5 kVA or 5 kVA system run my AC, freezer and pumping machine?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It depends on the total load and on what runs at the same time. LG lists a 9,000 BTU inverter split AC at 1,000 W rated cooling input and a 12,000 BTU unit at 1,090 W (1,350 W maximum). A 5 kVA inverter at a 0.8 power factor carries about 4 kW of real load, so always read the kW figure on the inverter's own datasheet. Fridges, freezers and pumping machines vary, so an installer should do a load audit from your rating plates."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is lithium better than tubular batteries?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "On the makers' own figures, the lithium model below is rated for four times the cycles of the tubular one, but compare the exact models. The Felicity LPBF48100-A manual states 6000 cycles at 80% depth of discharge, while a Luminous LPT 1240H tubular page states up to 1500 cycles at 80%, each on its maker's own test conditions. BusinessDay (February 2026) says lead-acid batteries last only three to five years. Ask for both options quoted side by side with the exact battery model written down."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I know an installer and the equipment are genuine?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "NEMSA guidelines as reported in April 2026 say rooftop solar PV must be installed by NEMSA-certified electrical contractors, and NEMSA publishes a directory and a verification page on nemsa.gov.ng. Ask for the competency certificate and look it up. Industry experts quoted by NAN in July 2026 named batteries and inverters as the most counterfeited items, so check serial numbers and warranty papers and have the exact models, warranty terms and VAT treatment written on the quote."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can I sell extra solar power back to the grid?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Not with a typical home system. NERC's Net Billing Regulations 2026 start eligibility at a renewable system of 50 kWp, with DisCo approval and a bidirectional meter, and a home system is far below that. Size your system for your own use."}}]}</script>
<style is:global>
  .rich p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: #555; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .rich ul { padding-left: 20px; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .rich li { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: #555; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .rich strong { color: #2B3A44; }
  .rich a { color: #B4501A; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .rich a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
</Fragment>

<!-- HERO -->
<section style="position:relative;min-height:560px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;overflow:hidden;">
  <img src="/images/hero-panorama.webp" alt="Nigeria landscape" width="2000" height="950" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high">
  <div style="position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(27,29,42,0.55) 0%, rgba(27,29,42,0.25) 55%, rgba(27,29,42,0.45) 100%);"></div>
  <div style="position:relative;max-width:880px;padding:96px 24px 130px;">
    <span style="display:inline-block;margin-bottom:18px;padding:7px 18px;border-radius:2px;font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.14);color:#fff;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.35);backdrop-filter:blur(3px);">Independent installers · Across Nigeria</span>
    <h1 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-weight:800;color:#fff;line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-0.015em;font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,58px);margin:0 0 18px;text-shadow:0 2px 24px rgba(27,29,42,0.45);">Solar for Home and Business in Nigeria, Quoted by Independent Installers</h1>
    <p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.92);max-width:640px;margin:0 auto 30px;text-shadow:0 1px 12px rgba(27,29,42,0.5);">Harmattan Solar Co is advertising for independent solar installers serving Lagos, Abuja, Port Harcourt, Ibadan, Benin City and Enugu. Call now with your location and what you want to run, and an installer will take your enquiry through a site survey to a written quote.</p>
    <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <a href="tel:+2348090000000" class="btn-green" style="font-size:15px;padding:16px 38px;">Call Now — +234 809 000 0000</a>
      <a href="/#contact" class="btn-white-outline" style="font-size:15px;">Get a Written Quote</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <svg class="swoosh" style="position:absolute;bottom:0;left:0;" viewBox="0 0 1440 70" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0,70 C360,10 1080,10 1440,70 L1440,70 L0,70 Z" fill="#ffffff"/></svg>
</section>

<!-- INTRO -->
<section style="padding:84px 24px 64px;background:#fff;">
  <div class="intro-grid" style="max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:0.9fr 1.1fr;gap:64px;align-items:center;">
    <div style="position:relative;">
      <div style="border-radius:18px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 24px 56px rgba(27,29,42,0.22);aspect-ratio:1/1;">
        <img src="/images/about.webp" alt="Harmattan Solar Co service crew" width="1024" height="1024" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
      </div>
      <div style="position:absolute;bottom:-18px;right:-14px;background:#B4501A;color:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:14px 22px;box-shadow:0 10px 26px rgba(180,80,26,0.4);">
        <p style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:800;margin:0;line-height:1;">1.5-10</p>
        <p style="font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;margin:4px 0 0;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;">kVA systems</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span class="kicker">Solar installation Nigeria</span>
      <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,40px);margin:0 0 18px;">Solar for home that you can check before you pay</h2>
      <div class="rich"><p>Most people reach for solar after the same run of events: light that comes and goes, and a gen that eats petrol to cover the gaps. As an illustration only, a 3.0 kVA generator running about 5 hours a day at about 1.25 litres an hour (Nigerian retailer Jamara Home says the Sumec Firman ECO4990ES runs up to 12 hours at 50% load on a 15 L tank, and 15 / 12 = 1.25) with petrol at N1,400 a litre (a Lagos pump price reported by Vanguard on 10-11 October 2026) costs 1.25 x 5 x 1,400 = N8,750 a day. That is an example, not a prediction for your house. Start with <a href="/home-solar-installation/">home solar installation</a> if you want a whole system, or <a href="/inverter-battery-installation/">inverter and battery installation</a> if you already have panels or an old inverter.</p><p>This site is advertising for independent Nigerian solar installers. It does not install or sell anything itself, and it holds no licence or certification of its own. What it does is help you ask for two or three comparable written quotes and give you the checks to run on each one. If you are weighing a business system, read <a href="/commercial-solar/">commercial solar</a> and the dated price ranges on <a href="/solar-system-price-nigeria/">solar system price in Nigeria</a> first, and see <a href="/solar-inverter-repair/">solar and inverter repair</a> if your current system keeps tripping.</p></div>
      <a href="/about/" class="btn-blue" style="margin-top:10px;">More About Us</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .intro-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; gap: 44px !important; } }
</style>

