<!-- AREAS -->
<section style="padding:76px 24px 60px;background:#fff;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center;">
    <span class="kicker">Service Areas</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,36px);margin:0 0 16px;">Serving Nigeria</h2>
    <div class="rich" style="text-align:left;"><p>Enquiries are taken for <a href="/solar-installation-lagos/">Lagos</a>, <a href="/solar-installation-abuja/">Abuja</a>, <a href="/solar-installation-port-harcourt/">Port Harcourt</a>, <a href="/solar-installation-ibadan/">Ibadan</a>, <a href="/solar-installation-benin-city/">Benin City</a> and <a href="/solar-installation-enugu/">Enugu</a>. Modelled panel output differs by city: PVGIS puts Abuja at about 1,534 kWh a year per kWp of panels and Port Harcourt at about 1,271, so the same panels do not produce the same energy everywhere. Each city page covers the local DisCo, the rainy-season dip and what to ask an installer there.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
<section style="padding:72px 24px;background:#FAF5EA;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3.5vw,36px);margin:0 0 32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(27,29,42,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 10px;">How much does solar for a home cost in Nigeria, and how is it scoped?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">It depends on the load you want to run, so an installer scopes it from the rating plates of your own appliances before quoting. For reference, Mercury Direct listed a 3.5 kVA hybrid inverter with 5 kWh of lithium and 8 x 450 W panels, installation included, at N3,400,000 in October 2026, and SMK Solar listed a 3.5 kVA, 5 kWh lithium and 6 x 450 W package at N3,121,000 (its page mentions installation accessories, so check whether labour is included). BusinessDay put 3-4 kVA systems at N2-3 million in February 2026. Naira prices move with the exchange rate, so a current written quote is the real number.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(27,29,42,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 10px;">How quickly will an installer respond, and how long does installation take?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">This site does not publish a guaranteed response or installation time, because the schedule belongs to the installer who quotes your job. Ask for the survey date and the installation schedule to be written on the proposal. A vague timeline on paper is a reason to compare with another quote.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(27,29,42,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 10px;">Will a 3.5 kVA or 5 kVA system run my AC, freezer and pumping machine?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">It depends on the total load and on what runs at the same time. LG lists a 9,000 BTU inverter split AC at 1,000 W rated cooling input and a 12,000 BTU unit at 1,090 W (1,350 W maximum). A 5 kVA inverter at a 0.8 power factor carries about 4 kW of real load, so always read the kW figure on the inverter's own datasheet. Fridges, freezers and pumping machines vary, so an installer should do a load audit from your rating plates.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(27,29,42,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 10px;">Is lithium better than tubular batteries?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">On the makers' own figures, the lithium model below is rated for four times the cycles of the tubular one, but compare the exact models. The Felicity LPBF48100-A manual states 6000 cycles at 80% depth of discharge, while a Luminous LPT 1240H tubular page states up to 1500 cycles at 80%, each on its maker's own test conditions. BusinessDay (February 2026) says lead-acid batteries last only three to five years. Ask for both options quoted side by side with the exact battery model written down.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(27,29,42,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 10px;">How do I know an installer and the equipment are genuine?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">NEMSA guidelines as reported in April 2026 say rooftop solar PV must be installed by NEMSA-certified electrical contractors, and NEMSA publishes a directory and a verification page on nemsa.gov.ng. Ask for the competency certificate and look it up. Industry experts quoted by NAN in July 2026 named batteries and inverters as the most counterfeited items, so check serial numbers and warranty papers and have the exact models, warranty terms and VAT treatment written on the quote.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(27,29,42,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 10px;">Can I sell extra solar power back to the grid?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Not with a typical home system. NERC's Net Billing Regulations 2026 start eligibility at a renewable system of 50 kWp, with DisCo approval and a bidirectional meter, and a home system is far below that. Size your system for your own use.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

